---
source: tests/surface_snapshots.rs
expression: "String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stdout)"
---
A note's kind is its folder, and is never a frontmatter field.
Fields are listed in canonical order; `mnemex` emits them this way.

project (projects/)
  purpose: A directory and repository of work; the entrypoint a session resolves to.
  status        required  enum: active | paused | completed | archived
  tags          optional  text list
  path          optional  text
  repo          optional  git remote
  body:
    ## Purpose

    ## Boundaries

    ## Notes

memory (memories/)
  purpose: Durable knowledge for one project that the repository, its git log, and its tracker cannot supply.
  project       required  wiki-link to project
  tags          optional  text list
  refs          optional  url list
  body:
    ## Summary

    ## Details

plan (plans/)
  purpose: A body of steps for one project; `open` until set `done`.
  project       required  wiki-link to project
  status        required  enum: open | done
  tags          optional  text list
  refs          optional  url list
  body:
    ## Goal

    ## Steps

    - [ ] 

adr (adrs/)
  purpose: A decision that constrains future work on one project.
  project       required  wiki-link to project
  status        required  enum: proposed | accepted | deprecated
  tags          optional  text list
  refs          optional  url list
  body:
    ## Context

    ## Decision

    ## Considered options

    ## Consequences

context (contexts/)
  purpose: The vocabulary and relationships of one project's bounded area.
  project       required  wiki-link to project
  tags          optional  text list
  body:
    ## Summary

    ## Language

    ## Relationships

    ## Example dialogue

    ## Flagged ambiguities
